BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Center for Continuing Medical Education] Stanford Medici
 ne Orthopaedic Academy: Pediatric and Adult ACL Update: Risk Factors\, Pre
 vention\, Surgical Reconstruction\, and Graft Options
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T130000
DTSTAMP:20260915T173023Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53205765566281-53205765566282@local-events
DESCRIPTION:OverviewThis CME activity provides an up-to-date\, clinically 
 practical review of anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) injury across pediatr
 ic and adult populations. Participants will gain a contemporary understand
 ing of risk factors\, evidence-based prevention strategies\, diagnostic ap
 proaches (physical examination and imaging)\, treatment options (nonoperat
 ive versus operative)\, graft choices for reconstruction\, and postoperati
 ve rehabilitation principles with the goal of optimizing patient outcomes
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseov
