UID:stanford_campus-law-10003271-1790254200-1790258400@law.stanford.edu-20
 26-09-24T12:50:00-07:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the American Constitution Society (ACS) and Stanford Coal
 ition for Abundance Law (SCALE) for a lunch discussion with Professor Nich
 olas Bagley (Michigan Law)\, whose 2021 Michigan Law Review article “The
  Procedure Fetish” argued that progressive commitments to procedural saf
 eguards\, transparency\, and adversarial process have hollowed out the gov
 ernment’s capacity to actually deliver on progressive goals. We’ll dis
 cuss where that argument leads for permitting\, regulatory reform\, and th
 e futur\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/when-pro
 cess-eats-progress-nicholas-bagley-on-the-procedure-fetish/\nLast synced: 
 2026-09-15 10:30 PDT
