BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Law] AI Initiative Speaker Series – Privilege Risk in 
 the Age of AI with Jina Choi\, Gibson Dunn
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T124500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T140000
DTSTAMP:20260915T173023Z
UID:stanford_campus-law-10003288-1791463500-1791468000@law.stanford.edu-20
 26-10-08T12:45:00-07:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Jina Choi\, a partner at Gibson Dunn and former Chief of the C
 orporate and Securities Fraud Division at the U.S. Attorney’s Office –
  Northern District of California\, examines how AI tools intersect with pr
 ivilege and confidentiality risks in legal practice. This discussion will 
 address the risks of putting client data into AI platforms\, the impact on
  privilege protections\, and what reps and warranties firms should require
  around data handling. Moderated by Professor Nate Persily.  \nRegister u
 sing\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/privilege-r
 isk-in-the-age-of-ai/\nLast synced: 2026-09-15 10:30 PDT
LOCATION:@ SLS: Room 270\, Crown Quadrangle\, 559 Nathan Abbott Way\, Stan
 ford\, CA\, 94305-8610\, United States
URL:https://law.stanford.edu/event/privilege-risk-in-the-age-of-ai/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Law] Rule of Law Speaker Series: AI and Political Freedo
 m
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T180000
DTSTAMP:20260915T173023Z
UID:stanford_campus-law-10003313-1791478800-1791482400@law.stanford.edu-20
 26-10-08T17:00:00-07:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:AI safety is having a moment. Once the preoccupation of techno
 logists and futurists\, it is now front-page news and kitchen-table conver
 sation. This is a welcome development. But there is one crucial dimension 
 the public conversation has yet to reach: the connection between AI safety
  and democracy. Without the political freedom that democracy secures\, AI 
 cannot and will not be safe. This point is urgent\, because AI is poised t
 o put unprecedented pressure on the very democratic institutions its sa\n
 \nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/rule-of-law-speak
 er-series-ai-and-political-freedom/\nLast synced: 2026-09-15 10:30 PDT
LOCATION:@ SLS: Room 190\, Crown Quadrangle 559 Nathan Abbott Way\, Stanfo
 rd\, CA\, 94305-8610\, United States
URL:https://law.stanford.edu/event/rule-of-law-speaker-series-ai-and-polit
 ical-freedom/
END:VEVENT
